@startuml regional-query
title US-12: Regional Query - Bounding Box Translated to H3 Cells, Only Relevant Chunks Scanned

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Express API /\nAlert Evaluator" as Caller
participant "H3 Library" as H3
database "TimescaleDB\nposition_history" as TSDB

Caller -> H3 : polyfill(bounding_box, resolution=5)

note over H3
  Translates the bounding box into
  the set of H3 cell IDs that overlap it.
  Done in application code before
  the query hits the database.
end note

H3 --> Caller : [ "8a2a1072b59ffff", "8a2a1072b4fffff", ... ]

Caller -> TSDB : SELECT entity_id, lat, lon, observed_at\nFROM position_history\nWHERE geo_cell IN ($cell_ids)\nAND observed_at BETWEEN $t1 AND $t2

note over TSDB
  Hypertable chunk exclusion applies to observed_at.
  Only chunks whose time range overlaps [$t1, $t2] are scanned.
  geo_cell IN ($cell_ids) index filter further narrows rows
  within the selected chunks.
  geo_cell is an indexed column, not a partition dimension.
  Unrelated time windows are excluded by chunk pruning alone.
end note

TSDB --> Caller : position rows for entities\nin region R during window T

note over Caller
  Query cost scales with the number of
  entities in the queried region and window,
  not with the total entity count in the system.
end note

@enduml
